From nobody Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:42:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] net/iavf: do not advertise runtime queue setup

Runtime queue setup corrupts queue state on an E810 VF. An Rx queue
that was stopped once never receives again, and the flow rule still
sends the stream to that queue, so the VF discards every packet of it.

Take RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_RX_QUEUE_SETUP and
RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_TX_QUEUE_SETUP away. The ethdev layer then
rejects a queue setup call on a running port, and an application must
set up each queue before it starts the port.

Signed-off-by: Marek Kasiewicz <marek.kasiewicz@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
index d601ec3b6a..e475b64971 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
@@ -1160,9 +1160,9 @@ iavf_dev_info_get(struct rte_eth_dev *dev, struct rte_eth_dev_info *dev_info)
 	dev_info->reta_size = vf->vf_res->rss_lut_size;
 	dev_info->flow_type_rss_offloads = IAVF_RSS_OFFLOAD_ALL;
 	dev_info->max_mac_addrs = IAVF_NUM_MACADDR_MAX;
-	dev_info->dev_capa =
-		RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_RX_QUEUE_SETUP |
-		RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_TX_QUEUE_SETUP;
+	/* Runtime queue setup corrupts E810 VF queue state. */
+	dev_info->dev_capa &= ~(RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_RX_QUEUE_SETUP |
+				RTE_ETH_DEV_CAPA_RUNTIME_TX_QUEUE_SETUP);
 	dev_info->rx_offload_capa =
 		RTE_ETH_RX_OFFLOAD_VLAN_STRIP |
 		RTE_ETH_RX_OFFLOAD_QINQ_STRIP |
